<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman ups BCH to &quot;neutral&quot;.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Lehman ups BCH to &quot;neutral&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Central Hispano was raised to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;underperform&quot; at Lehman Brothers, the investment bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Raising estimates for 1997 net profit to 52.5 billion pesetas from 50.5 billion to reflect continuing good cost controls, Lehman said the upgrade had a positive knock-on effect on longer-term prospects.</p>
<p>Analyst Sheila Garrard said she now considered the stock to be &quot;fully valued.&quot;</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
